<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michael Aung-Thwin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Michael Aung-Thwin is a historian of Myanmar, long a professor at the University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>. In his studies of the Pagan Kingdom he argued that the growth of tax-free religious land gradually weakened the state, and in The Mists of Ramanna (2005) he questioned the traditional account of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anawrahta">Anawrahta</a>'s conquest of Thaton and the extent of early Mon influence on Pagan.</p></div>
